Q4: exact means E[c3], E[c5], E[alpha2] over the uniform tiling measure (brute n<=7)
================================================================================
  n   E[c3]            E[c5]            E[alpha2]        (exact Fractions)
  3   1/2              0                0                [c3 closed-form (C(n,3)+(n-2))/4 = 1/2  match=True]
  4   3/2              0                0                [c3 closed-form (C(n,3)+(n-2))/4 = 3/2  match=True]
  5   13/4             19/16            0                [c3 closed-form (C(n,3)+(n-2))/4 = 13/4  match=True]
  6   6                49/8             15/16            [c3 closed-form (C(n,3)+(n-2))/4 = 6  match=True]
  7   10               315/16           93/16            [c3 closed-form (C(n,3)+(n-2))/4 = 10  match=True]

================================================================================
Q4b: derive E[c5] and E[alpha2] closed forms via per-subset linearity (the THM-554 template)
================================================================================
  E[c5] = sum over 5-subsets S of E[# directed 5-cycles on S].
  Per-subset term depends on HOW MANY of the 10 internal pairs are base-path arcs
  (those are FIXED, contributing a 'consecutive-run' structure). Compute exactly:
    n=5: E[c5] = 19/16 = 1.1875
    n=6: E[c5] = 49/8 = 6.1250
    n=7: E[c5] = 315/16 = 19.6875
    n=8: E[c5] = 199/4 = 49.7500
  E[alpha2] (3-cycle x 3-cycle disjoint pairs leading term, n>=6):
  = sum over disjoint vertex-set pairs (T1,T2) of P[3cyc on T1]*P[3cyc on T2]
  + (cross terms with 5-cycles for n>=8). Leading (triangle-pair) part:
    n=6: E[#disjoint 3-cycle pairs] = 15/16 = 0.9375
    n=7: E[#disjoint 3-cycle pairs] = 93/16 = 5.8125
    n=8: E[#disjoint 3-cycle pairs] = 173/8 = 21.6250

[saved 05-knowledge/results/tiling_gf_beyond-scores-to-OCF_kps-Sx-wf.out]

